  "live_records": {
    "q-276297": {
      "dom_id": "step-q276297",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "A fair spinner has six sides labeled with the numbers $-2,$ $-1,$ $0,$ $1,$ $2,$ and $3.$ If the spinner is spun, what is the expected value of the outcome?\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the outcome of the spinner. Then the support is $S=\\{-2,-1,0,1,2,3\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{6}:$\n\n$$\nf(-2)=f(-1)=f(0)=f(1)=f(2)=f(3)=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =-2\\cdot f(-2)+(-1)\\cdot f(-1)+0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{1}{6})+(-1)(\\frac{1}{6})+0(\\frac{1}{6})+1(\\frac{1}{6})+2(\\frac{1}{6})+3(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{6}-\\frac{1}{6}+0+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{2}{6}+\\frac{3}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-1+0+1+2+3}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
