    "q-89152": {
      "dom_id": "step-q89152",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "A fair spinner has six sides each labeled $-2,$ $-1,$ $1,$ $3,$ $5,$ and $6.$ If spinner is spun, what is its expected value?",
      "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the spin of the fair spinner. Then the support is $S=\\{-2,-1,1,3,5,6\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{6}:$\n\n$$\nf(-2)=f(-1)=f(1)=f(3)=f(5)=f(6)=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =(-2)\\cdot f(-2)+(-1)\\cdot f(-1)+1\\cdot f(1)+3\\cdot f(3)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =(-2)(\\frac{1}{6})+(-1)(\\frac{1}{6})+1(\\frac{1}{6})+3(\\frac{1}{6})+5(\\frac{1}{6})+6(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{6}+\\frac{-1}{6}+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{3}{6}+\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{6}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-1+1+3+5+6}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
