    "q-83981": {
      "dom_id": "step-q83981",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "A stack contains four cards, where each card is labeled $1$, $4$, $6$, or $9.$ If one card is randomly drawn, what is its expected value?",
      "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the label on a randomly drawn card. Then the support is $S=\\{1,4,6,9\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{4}:$\n\n$$\nf(1)=f(4)=f(6)=f(9)=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+4\\cdot f(4)+6\\cdot f(6)+9\\cdot f(9) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{4})+4(\\frac{1}{4})+6(\\frac{1}{4})+9(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{4}{4}+\\frac{6}{4}+\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+4+6+9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{4} \\\\  & =5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
