    "q-89150": {
      "dom_id": "step-q89150",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "What is the expected value of one roll of a four-sided die?",
      "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the roll of a four-sided die. Then the support is $S=\\{1,2,3,4\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{4}:$\n\n$$\nf(1)=f(2)=f(3)=f(4)=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)++3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{4})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{1}{4})+4(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{2}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{4}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+2+3+4}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{4} \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
