    "q-84020": {
      "dom_id": "step-q84020",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The number of heads facing upward after tossing $2$ unfair coins follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected value of the number of heads facing upward after tossing the $2$ coins?\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{4}{9}$ | $\\frac{4}{9}$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{9})+1(\\frac{4}{9})+2(\\frac{4}{9}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{4}{9}+\\frac{8}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+8}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
