      "kp_id": "e-7383"
    },
    "q-127259": {
      "dom_id": "step-q127259",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "The rolls of an unfair octahedral die follow the probability mass function $f(x)$ as shown in the table below. What is the expected value of one roll of the die?\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{32}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{32}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{8})+2(\\frac{1}{16})+3(\\frac{1}{16})+4(\\frac{3}{32})+5(\\frac{1}{8})+6(\\frac{1}{32})+7(\\frac{1}{4})+8(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{2}{16}+\\frac{3}{16}+\\frac{12}{32}+\\frac{5}{8}+\\frac{6}{32}+\\frac{7}{4}+\\frac{8}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{32}+\\frac{4}{32}+\\frac{6}{32}+\\frac{12}{32}+\\frac{20}{32}+\\frac{6}{32}+\\frac{56}{32}+\\frac{64}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+4+6+12+20+6+56+64}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{172}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{43}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
