    "q-337038": {
      "dom_id": "step-q337038",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "The number of heads facing upward after tossing $3$ unfair coins follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected value of the number of heads facing upward after tossing the $3$ coins? Do not round the answer.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{2}{9})+1(\\frac{1}{3})+2(\\frac{1}{9})+3(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{2}{9}+1 \\\\  & =0+\\frac{3}{9}+\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{9}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+3+2+9}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
