    "q-337188": {
      "dom_id": "step-q337188",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "The sum of the outcomes of one roll of two unfair four-sided dice follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected value of the sum of the outcomes for one roll of the two dice?\n\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{3}{40}$ | $\\frac{7}{40}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{20}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5) \\\\  & \\,\\,+6\\cdot f(6)+7\\cdot f(7)+8\\cdot f(8) \\\\  & =2(\\frac{3}{40})+3(\\frac{7}{40})+4(\\frac{1}{5})+5(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & \\,\\,+6(\\frac{3}{20})+7(\\frac{1}{10})+8(\\frac{1}{20}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{40}+\\frac{21}{40}+\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{5}{4}+\\frac{18}{20}+\\frac{7}{10}+\\frac{8}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{40}+\\frac{21}{40}+\\frac{32}{40}+\\frac{50}{40}+\\frac{36}{40}+\\frac{28}{40}+\\frac{16}{40} \\\\  & =\\frac{6+21+32+50+36+28+16}{40} \\\\  & =\\frac{189}{40} \\\\  & =4.725.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
