    "q-337204": {
      "dom_id": "step-q337204",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "A stack of cards has $2$ cards labeled with four and $6$ cards labeled with ten. If one card is randomly drawn from the stack, what is its expected value?\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the value labeled on a randomly drawn card. Then the support is $S=\\{4,10\\}.$\n\nIn the stack there are $2$ cards labeled with four and $6$ cards labeled with ten (eight cards in total), so the probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(4) & =\\frac{2}{8}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(10) & =\\frac{6}{8}=\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =4\\cdot f(4)+10\\cdot f(10) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{4})+10(\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{15}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
