    "q-84067": {
      "dom_id": "step-q84067",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Several children were asked how many siblings they have. The number of siblings of each child was recorded below. If $X$ is the number of siblings of a randomly selected child, what is the expected value of $X?$\n\n| Number of siblings | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Number of Children | $1$ | $5$ | $3$ | $1$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the number of siblings, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of children is $1+5+3+1=10,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0)=f(0) & =\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ P(X=1)=f(1) & =\\frac{5}{10}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ P(X=2)=f(2) & =\\frac{3}{10} \\\\ P(X=3)=f(3) & =\\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{10})+1(\\frac{1}{2})+2(\\frac{3}{10})+3(\\frac{1}{10}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{5}{10}+\\frac{6}{10}+\\frac{3}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+5+6+3}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{10} \\\\  & =1.4\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
