    "q-276300": {
      "dom_id": "step-q276300",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "A quality control manager at a warehouse inspects electronic boxes for defective items. The number of faulty items in each box was recorded and summarized below. If $X$ is the number of faulty items in a box, what is the expected value of $X?$\n\n| Number of Boxes | $13$ | $6$ | $4$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Faulty Items | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the faulty items, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of boxes is $13+6+4+2=25,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0)=f(0) & =\\frac{13}{25} \\\\ P(X=1)=f(1) & =\\frac{6}{25} \\\\ P(X=2)=f(2) & =\\frac{4}{25} \\\\ P(X=3)=f(3) & =\\frac{2}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{13}{25}$ | $\\frac{6}{25}$ | $\\frac{4}{25}$ | $\\frac{2}{25}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{13}{25})+1(\\frac{6}{25})+2(\\frac{4}{25})+3(\\frac{2}{25}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{25}+\\frac{8}{25}+\\frac{6}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{6+8+6}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
