    "q-89157": {
      "dom_id": "step-q89157",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Several households were asked the number of children that lived there. The number of children in each was recorded below. If $X$ is the number of children that live at a randomly selected household, what is the expected value of $X?$\n\n| Number of Children | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Number of Households | $6$ | $9$ | $6$ | $3$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the number of childen, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of households is $3+9+6+6=24,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=1)=f(1) & =\\frac{6}{24}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(X=2)=f(2) & =\\frac{9}{24}=\\frac{3}{8} \\\\ P(X=3)=f(3) & =\\frac{6}{24}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(X=4)=f(4) & =\\frac{3}{24}=\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{4})+2(\\frac{3}{8})+3(\\frac{1}{4})+4(\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{2}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+3+3+2}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =2.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
